# Blueprint A — Study Buddy Embedded on Course Page

**Feature:** Every course page gets a dedicated Study Buddy tab. When a student opens it, Study Buddy automatically loads all materials for that course and surfaces tools built for it. No setup required — the course context powers everything.

**Codex model:** claude-sonnet-4-6
**Scope:** Feature addition — no new DB models required. Touches 2 existing files, adds 1 new component, updates 1 API route.

---

## What Already Exists (do not rebuild)

- **Course page:** `app/courses/page.tsx` — single-page app with tab system. Current tabs: `materials | tools | discussion | submissions | pulse | map | settings`
- **TabId type** (line 44): `type TabId = 'materials' | 'tools' | 'discussion' | 'submissions' | 'pulse' | 'map' | 'settings'`
- **StudyBuddyInterface:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx` — full Study Buddy UI with 7 modes (tutor, quiz, flashcards, socratic, teach-back, debate, essay)
- **Chat API:** `app/api/chat/route.ts` — already accepts `courseId` param and injects syllabus context + learning objectives. Has STUDY_BUDDY mode handling.
- **CourseMaterial model** (prisma schema line 587): `{ id, courseId, title, content, materialType, moduleNumber, isVisible }`
- **CourseToolLink model** — links tools to courses. Course page already fetches linked tools in the `tools` tab.
- **Platform Study Buddy tool** — there is a seeded STUDY_BUDDY tool in the DB (find its ID from seed data or query `Tool.findFirst({ where: { toolType: 'STUDY_BUDDY' } })`)

---

## What Needs to Be Built

### 1. New tab on course page

**File:** `app/courses/page.tsx`

Add `'study'` to the TabId union:
```typescript
type TabId = 'materials' | 'tools' | 'discussion' | 'submissions' | 'pulse' | 'map' | 'settings' | 'study'
```

Add the tab button in the tab bar alongside the others. Use a `Bot` or `Sparkles` icon from lucide-react. Only show to students and educators (not hidden, but visually de-emphasised for settings-only admins). Label: **"Study"**.

Tab order: `materials → study → tools → discussion → ...rest`

### 2. Study tab content panel

**File:** `app/courses/page.tsx` (inside the tab content switch/conditional)

When `activeTab === 'study'`, render:

```tsx
<CourseStudyPanel
  courseId={selectedCourse.id}
  courseName={selectedCourse.title}
  courseCode={selectedCourse.courseCode}
  userEmail={currentUser.email}
  linkedTools={linkedTools} // already fetched for the tools tab
/>
```

### 3. New component: CourseStudyPanel

**File:** `app/components/courses/CourseStudyPanel.tsx` (create new)

This component is the shell around StudyBuddyInterface for the course context. It:

1. Fetches the platform Study Buddy tool ID on mount:
   ```
   GET /api/tools?type=STUDY_BUDDY&platform=true
   ```
   Or hardcode the platform Study Buddy tool ID as a constant if simpler — query `Tool` where `toolType = 'STUDY_BUDDY'` and name contains "Study Buddy".

2. Renders a two-column layout:
   - **Left (2/3 width):** `<StudyBuddyInterface>` with `toolId` + `courseId` passed
   - **Right (1/3 width):** Course Tools launcher panel (see below)

3. Passes `courseId` to StudyBuddyInterface as a new prop (see section 4).

**Layout sketch:**
```
┌─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────┐
│                             │  Tools for this  │
│   StudyBuddyInterface       │  course          │
│   (courseId auto-loaded)    │  ──────────────  │
│                             │  [Tool Card]     │
│                             │  [Tool Card]     │
│                             │  [Tool Card]     │
│                             │                  │
└─────────────────────────────┴──────────────────┘
```

**Course Tools launcher (right panel):**
- Title: "Tools for [courseCode]"
- List of `linkedTools` (already available from parent)
- Each tool: icon, name, short description, "Launch →" button that opens `/tools/[id]`
- If no linked tools: "No tools linked to this course yet." (educator sees a "+ Link a tool" button)
- Keep it simple — no pagination, just a scrollable list

### 4. Add courseId prop to StudyBuddyInterface

**File:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx`

Add `courseId?: string` to `StudyBuddyInterfaceProps`.

Pass it through to the `/api/chat` POST body:
```typescript
body: JSON.stringify({
  toolId,
  messages: ...,
  sessionId,
  mode,
  courseId, // ADD THIS
}),
```

Also pass it to `/api/sessions` POST on mount so the session is linked to the course:
```typescript
body: JSON.stringify({ toolId, courseId }),
```

When `courseId` is present, update the welcome message on the mode selection screen to reflect the course:
```
"Studying [courseName]. Choose how you want to learn."
```
Display the course name as a small pill/badge in the header of the select screen.

### 5. Update chat API to inject CourseMaterial content for Study Buddy

**File:** `app/api/chat/route.ts`

The API already handles `courseId` (lines 122–154) for syllabus context and learning objectives. It does NOT currently load `CourseMaterial` records for Study Buddy.

**Add this block inside the `if (isStudyBuddy)` section (after the existing ToolDocument fetch):**

```typescript
// Pull course materials if courseId is provided
if (courseId) {
  const courseMaterials = await prisma.courseMaterial.findMany({
    where: { courseId: String(courseId), isVisible: true },
    select: { title: true, content: true, moduleNumber: true, materialType: true },
    orderBy: [{ moduleNumber: 'asc' }, { createdAt: 'asc' }],
  }).catch(() => [])

  if (courseMaterials.length > 0) {
    let courseMatContext = ''
    let charCount = 0
    for (const mat of courseMaterials) {
      const section = `\n\n--- ${mat.moduleNumber ? `Module ${mat.moduleNumber}: ` : ''}${mat.title} ---\n${mat.content}`
      if (charCount + section.length > 80000) break // leave room for ToolDocuments
      courseMatContext += section
      charCount += section.length
    }
    // Prepend course materials before any uploaded ToolDocuments
    systemPrompt = `${modePrompt}${toolContext}\n\n## Course Materials\n${courseMatContext}`
  }
}
```

The existing ToolDocument injection remains — it appends after course materials. Total context budget stays at 120K chars.

---

## Files to Modify

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `app/courses/page.tsx` | Add `'study'` to TabId, add tab button, add tab panel rendering `<CourseStudyPanel>` |
| `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx` | Add `courseId` prop, pass to `/api/chat` and `/api/sessions`, update welcome UI |
| `app/api/chat/route.ts` | Inject `CourseMaterial` records into Study Buddy context when `courseId` provided |

## Files to Create

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app/components/courses/CourseStudyPanel.tsx` | Shell component — fetches Study Buddy toolId, renders split layout with StudyBuddyInterface + course tools launcher |

---

## API needed (may already exist)

**Get platform Study Buddy tool:**
```
GET /api/tools?type=STUDY_BUDDY
```
Check if `app/api/tools/route.ts` supports a `type` query param filter. If not, add it:
```typescript
if (searchParams.get('type')) {
  where.toolType = searchParams.get('type') as ToolType
}
```
Return the first result. The component uses this toolId for all course-level Study Buddy sessions.

---

## Behavior Summary

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| Student opens course → Study tab | Study Buddy loads with course materials pre-injected, all 7 modes available |
| Student picks Quiz mode | AI generates questions from course materials only |
| Student uploads personal notes | Added on top of course materials (existing behavior) |
| Educator opens course → Study tab | Same experience — can test the Study Buddy as their students will see it |
| Course has linked tools | Right panel shows them with launch buttons |
| Course has no linked tools | Right panel shows empty state with link prompt for educators |

---

## Do Not Build (out of scope for this blueprint)

- Student notes / notebook (Blueprint C)
- Course switcher in standalone Study Buddy (Blueprint B)
- Modifying the Sandy concierge behavior
- Any new DB migrations
