<file path="Blueprints/B-study-buddy-course-switcher.md">
# Blueprint B — Study Buddy Standalone: Course Switcher + "Which Course?" Flow

**Feature:** When a student opens Study Buddy from the marketplace (not from a course page), they get a course selector that lets them attach course materials to their session. Options: a specific course, None, Manual upload, or Web only. They can switch courses mid-session.

**Codex model:** claude-sonnet-4-6
**Scope:** Feature addition — no new DB models. Touches StudyBuddyInterface and adds one small API endpoint. The course-page embedded version (Blueprint A) is unaffected.

---

## What Already Exists (do not rebuild)

- **StudyBuddyInterface:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx` — 3 screens (select/chat/wrapup), 7 modes, doc upload
- **Course enrollment:** `CourseEnrollment` model links students to courses. `GET /api/courses` returns courses for the current user.
- **Chat API:** `app/api/chat/route.ts` accepts `courseId` and loads `CourseMaterial` records (added in Blueprint A). If Blueprint A is not yet done, that injection must be done as part of this blueprint.
- **Auth header:** All API calls use `x-demo-user-email` header — the user's enrolled courses can be fetched with this.

---

## Context Modes

A student in standalone Study Buddy can be in one of four **context modes**:

| Mode | Value | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| A specific course | `{ type: 'course', courseId, courseName }` | Chat API receives `courseId`, injects CourseMaterial |
| None | `{ type: 'none' }` | No course context. AI answers from general knowledge. |
| Manual | `{ type: 'manual' }` | Student uploads their own docs. Existing ToolDocument flow. |
| Web only | `{ type: 'web' }` | Prompt instructs AI to draw from general knowledge, no docs. |

---

## What Needs to Be Built

### 1. Course context state in StudyBuddyInterface

**File:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx`

**Condition:** This flow ONLY applies when `courseId` prop is NOT passed (i.e., standalone/marketplace launch). When `courseId` prop IS passed (course page embed from Blueprint A), skip this entirely and go straight to the existing behavior.

Add state:
```typescript
type ContextMode =
  | { type: 'course'; courseId: string; courseName: string; courseCode: string }
  | { type: 'none' }
  | { type: 'manual' }
  | { type: 'web' }
  | null // null = not yet chosen

const [contextMode, setContextMode] = useState<ContextMode>(null)
const [enrolledCourses, setEnrolledCourses] = useState<{ id: string; title: string; courseCode: string }[]>([])
const [loadingCourses, setLoadingCourses] = useState(false)
```

### 2. Fetch enrolled courses on mount (standalone only)

When component mounts and `courseId` prop is absent:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (courseId) return // Blueprint A path — skip
  setLoadingCourses(true)
  fetch('/api/courses', { headers: { 'x-demo-user-email': userEmail } })
    .then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : [])
    .then(data => setEnrolledCourses(data.courses ?? data ?? []))
    .catch(() => {})
    .finally(() => setLoadingCourses(false))
}, [courseId, userEmail])
```

### 3. Context picker screen (new screen before mode select)

**When to show:** `courseId` prop is absent AND `contextMode === null`

Show BEFORE the mode selection screen. This is inserted as a new initial screen.

**UI:**

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Study Buddy                                │
│  Which course are we studying?              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                             │
│  Your Courses                               │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ 📚 TEK-100  Introduction to...  →   │   │
│  │ 📚 CHEM-210 Organic Chemistry   →   │   │
│  │ 📚 LAW-756  Evidence            →   │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                             │
│  ──────── or ────────                       │
│                                             │
│  [ No course — general study ]              │
│  [ Upload my own materials   ]              │
│  [ Web / general knowledge   ]              │
│                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Each enrolled course row: shows `courseCode`, truncated `title`, arrow. Clicking sets `contextMode = { type: 'course', courseId, courseName, courseCode }` and advances to mode select screen.

The three alternative options at bottom:
- **No course** → `contextMode = { type: 'none' }` → advance to mode select
- **Upload my own** → `contextMode = { type: 'manual' }` → advance to mode select (docs panel opens automatically)
- **Web / general** → `contextMode = { type: 'web' }` → advance to mode select

If `loadingCourses` is true, show a spinner row in the course list.
If no enrolled courses, hide the "Your Courses" section and show only the three alternatives.

### 4. Course context badge on the mode select screen

**File:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx` — select screen header

When `contextMode` is set and is not null, show a context badge beneath the "How do you want to study today?" subtitle:

```
[ 📚 TEK-100 · Introduction to Engineering  ×change ]
```

- Click "change" → reset `contextMode` to null (returns to context picker)
- For `none` → badge reads "No course context"
- For `manual` → badge reads "Personal materials"
- For `web` → badge reads "General knowledge"

### 5. Course context badge on the chat screen

In the chat header bar (alongside the mode pills), show a small course pill:

```
[ ← ] [ Explain It ] [ Quiz Me ] ... [ TEK-100 ▾ ] [ End ]
```

The `TEK-100 ▾` pill is a dropdown/button. Clicking it opens a compact popover:
- Lists enrolled courses (same list as context picker)
- "No course", "Manual", "Web" options
- Selecting a new course: sets `contextMode`, clears messages, reloads the session (so new course materials are injected)

This is the **easy switching** experience. One click to flip courses mid-study.

### 6. Pass contextMode to chat API

In the `sendMessage` function, use `contextMode` to determine what `courseId` to send:

```typescript
const activeCourseId =
  courseId ?? // Blueprint A: prop takes precedence
  (contextMode?.type === 'course' ? contextMode.courseId : undefined)

// Build the request body
const chatBody: Record<string, unknown> = {
  toolId,
  messages: history.map(m => ({ role: m.role, content: m.content })),
  sessionId,
  mode,
}

if (activeCourseId) chatBody.courseId = activeCourseId

if (contextMode?.type === 'web') {
  chatBody.webMode = true // signal to API: general knowledge, no docs
}
```

### 7. Handle webMode in the chat API

**File:** `app/api/chat/route.ts`

Add to the `if (isStudyBuddy)` block:

```typescript
const { webMode } = body

if (webMode) {
  // Override mode prompt to use general knowledge
  const modePrompt = STUDY_BUDDY_MODES[mode] || STUDY_BUDDY_MODES.tutor
  systemPrompt = `${modePrompt}\n\nNote: The student is studying from general knowledge — no specific course materials are loaded. Answer from your broad knowledge base.`
  // Skip document loading
} else {
  // existing ToolDocument + CourseMaterial injection
}
```

### 8. Docs panel behavior per context mode

| Context mode | Docs panel behavior |
|---|---|
| `course` | Show course docs (read-only, labeled "course") + allow student to add personal uploads on top |
| `none` | Show only student uploads. Course badge absent. |
| `manual` | Docs panel opens automatically. Prompt: "Upload your materials to get started." |
| `web` | Docs panel hidden entirely. Show a small note: "Using general knowledge — no documents." |

---

## API: GET /api/courses

**File:** `app/api/courses/route.ts` (likely exists — verify it returns enrolled courses for the current user)

The response should include at minimum: `{ courses: [{ id, courseCode, title }] }`

If the current endpoint returns all courses (not filtered by enrollment), add enrollment filtering:
```typescript
const enrollments = await prisma.courseEnrollment.findMany({
  where: { userId: user.id },
  include: { course: { select: { id: true, courseCode: true, title: true } } },
})
return NextResponse.json(enrollments.map(e => e.course))
```

---

## Files to Modify

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx` | Add `ContextMode` state, context picker screen, course badge on select/chat screens, pass courseId/webMode to API |
| `app/api/chat/route.ts` | Handle `webMode` flag |
| `app/api/courses/route.ts` | Verify/add enrollment filtering so enrolled courses are returned |

---

## Screen Flow

```
[Standalone launch from /tools/[id]]
           ↓
  [Context picker screen]        ← NEW
  Pick course / none / manual / web
           ↓
  [Mode select screen]           ← existing (+ context badge)
  Pick: Explain / Quiz / Socratic / etc.
           ↓
  [Chat screen]                  ← existing (+ course switcher pill)
           ↓
  [Wrap-up screen]               ← existing
```

---

## Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Student has no enrolled courses | Show only the three alternatives (no course/manual/web). No empty course list. |
| Student switches course mid-chat | Warn with a subtle toast: "Switching course will clear this chat." Clear messages, reload session. |
| courseId prop passed (Blueprint A) | Skip context picker entirely. `contextMode` never used. |
| Student picks same course they're already on | No-op, close the switcher |
| API request with no courseId + no webMode | Falls back to ToolDocument-only context (existing behavior) |

---

## Do Not Build (out of scope)

- Student notes / notebook (Blueprint C)
- Course page Study Buddy embed (Blueprint A)
- Modifying Sandy
- New DB migrations
</file>

<file path="Blueprints/C-student-notebook.md">
# Blueprint C — Student Notebook

**Feature:** Students can ask Sandy to save notes mid-conversation. Sandy asks a clarifying question ("Is this for Organic Chemistry?"), creates a structured note, and it appears in a Notebook feed on the student's home dashboard. Notes are editable. Students can optionally transfer a note into a tool's knowledge base with one click.

**Codex model:** claude-sonnet-4-6
**Scope:** New feature. Requires 1 new DB model (`StudentNote`), 1 migration, 2 new API routes, 1 new component, changes to Sandy (concierge API), and changes to the home dashboard.

---

## What Already Exists (do not rebuild)

- **Sandy / ConciergePanel:** `app/components/ConciergePanel.tsx` — global sidebar AI. Uses `app/api/concierge/route.ts`. Sandy is page-aware via `currentPage` param.
- **Home dashboard:** `app/page.tsx` — student view has Learning Vitals grid, recent sessions, badges, QuestPanel. Right column has QuestPanel.
- **UserMemory model:** Already exists for personalization — NOT the right model for notes (notes are user-facing content, memories are AI personalization hints).
- **Auth:** `x-demo-user-email` header on all requests.
- **StudyBuddyInterface:** Has document upload — notes transferred to knowledge base will use the existing upload flow (`POST /api/study/[toolId]/upload`).

---

## New DB Model

**File:** `prisma/schema.prisma`

Add after the `UserMemory` model:

```prisma
model StudentNote {
  id         String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId     String
  user       User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  title      String                         // Sandy generates or student sets
  content    String   @db.Text             // Full note body (markdown ok)
  courseId   String?                        // Optional course association
  course     Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
  source     String   @default("sandy")    // "sandy" | "manual"
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([userId, createdAt])
  @@index([userId, courseId])
}
```

Add the reverse relation on `User`:
```prisma
notes  StudentNote[]
```

Add the reverse relation on `Course`:
```prisma
studentNotes  StudentNote[]
