### 1.2 — Quiz Score Tracking

**Problem:** After a quiz session, students have no idea how many questions they got right. The wrap-up screen says "You exchanged N messages" — a meaningless metric.

**Approach:** Parse AI feedback to detect correct/incorrect outcomes. Store a running score in state. Show on wrap-up screen.

**File:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx`

**Step A — Add score state:**
```typescript
const [quizScore, setQuizScore] = useState<{ correct: number; total: number }>({ correct: 0, total: 0 })
```
Reset on mode change: in `enterMode`, add `setQuizScore({ correct: 0, total: 0 })`.

**Step B — Detect outcomes after each AI response in quiz mode:**
After the streaming loop completes in `sendMessage`, add detection logic:
```typescript
// After the while(true) streaming loop, before the catch block:
if (mode === 'quiz' && fullText) {
  const lower = fullText.toLowerCase()
  // Detect explicit correctness signals in the AI response
  const isCorrect = /\b(correct!|that'?s right|well done|exactly right|yes,? that'?s|great job)\b/.test(lower)
  const isIncorrect = /\b(not quite|incorrect|that'?s not|wrong|actually,? the (correct|right)|try again)\b/.test(lower)
  // Only count if this was a response to a user answer (not the initial question)
  // We detect this by checking if the prior user message looked like an answer choice (A/B/C/D or short text)
  const lastUserMsg = history.filter(m => m.role === 'user').at(-1)?.content ?? ''
  const looksLikeAnswer = /^[A-D]$|^[A-D][).]/i.test(lastUserMsg.trim()) || lastUserMsg.trim().split(' ').length <= 8
  if (looksLikeAnswer && (isCorrect || isIncorrect)) {
    setQuizScore(prev => ({
      correct: prev.correct + (isCorrect ? 1 : 0),
      total: prev.total + 1,
    }))
  }
}
```

**Step C — Show score on wrap-up screen:**
In the wrapup screen JSX (around line 509), replace the generic message count paragraph:

```tsx
<p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6 text-center">
  Great work! You exchanged {messageCount} message{messageCount !== 1 ? 's' : ''} in{' '}
  <span className={`font-medium ${currentModeConfig.color}`}>{currentModeConfig.label}</span> mode.
</p>
```

With a conditional block:
```tsx
{mode === 'quiz' && quizScore.total > 0 ? (
  <div className="text-center mb-6">
    <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">
      {quizScore.correct}/{quizScore.total}
    </p>
    <p className="text-sm text-gray-500">
      questions correct in{' '}
      <span className={`font-medium ${currentModeConfig.color}`}>{currentModeConfig.label}</span> mode
    </p>
    {quizScore.total >= 5 && (
      <p className="text-xs mt-1 text-gray-400">
        {Math.round((quizScore.correct / quizScore.total) * 100)}% accuracy
      </p>
    )}
  </div>
) : (
  <p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6 text-center">
    Great work! You exchanged {messageCount} message{messageCount !== 1 ? 's' : ''} in{' '}
    <span className={`font-medium ${currentModeConfig.color}`}>{currentModeConfig.label}</span> mode.
  </p>
)}
```

Also reset score in the "Study Again" and "Switch Mode" buttons: add `setQuizScore({ correct: 0, total: 0 })` alongside `setMessages([])`.

**Acceptance criteria:**
- Run a quiz session with 5 questions → wrap-up shows `3/5` (or whatever the correct count is)
- Non-quiz modes still show the existing message count copy
- Score resets when you hit "Study Again"

**Note:** Regex-based score detection is approximate — it depends on consistent AI phrasing. If false positives occur, tighten the regex or add a note to the wrap-up: "Score is estimated based on AI feedback phrasing."

