### 1.3 — Flashcard Mode Gets a Card UI

**Problem:** Flashcards render as plain chat bubbles. Students can see both question and answer simultaneously, defeating the purpose. The mode needs a distinct visual treatment.

**Approach:** Detect when a flashcard response contains a "front" and "back" using a separator pattern. If detected, render as a flippable card. If not detected, fall back to normal bubble rendering.

**File:** `app/components/StudyBuddyInterface.tsx`

**Step A — Add flip state:**
```typescript
const [flippedCards, setFlippedCards] = useState<Set<string>>(new Set())
```
Reset in `enterMode`: `setFlippedCards(new Set())`.

**Step B — Add a card detection helper** (near `extractMultipleChoiceOptions`):
```typescript
function extractFlashcard(text: string): { front: string; back: string } | null {
  // Match patterns like:
  // **Term:** ... \n**Definition:** ...
  // Q: ... \nA: ...
  // Front: ... \nBack: ...
  const patterns = [
    /\*\*(?:Term|Front|Question)\*\*[:\s]+(.+?)[\n\r]+\*\*(?:Definition|Back|Answer)\*\*[:\s]+([\s\S]+)/i,
    /^(?:Term|Front|Q)[:\s]+(.+?)[\n\r]+(?:Definition|Back|A)[:\s]+([\s\S]+)/im,
  ]
  for (const pattern of patterns) {
    const match = text.trim().match(pattern)
    if (match) {
      return { front: match[1].trim(), back: match[2].trim() }
    }
  }
  return null
}
```

**Step C — Render flashcard UI** in the messages map, for assistant messages in flashcard mode. Replace the standard assistant bubble rendering with:

```tsx
{msg.role === 'assistant' && mode === 'flashcards' && (() => {
  const card = extractFlashcard(msg.content)
  if (!card) return null // fall through to standard rendering below
  const isFlipped = flippedCards.has(msg.id)
  return (
    <div className="ml-11">
      <div className="bg-white border-2 border-emerald-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm max-w-sm">
        <div className="px-5 py-4">
          <p className="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">
            {isFlipped ? 'Definition' : 'Term'}
          </p>
          <p className="text-sm text-gray-900 font-medium leading-snug">
            {isFlipped ? card.back : card.front}
          </p>
        </div>
        <button
          onClick={() => setFlippedCards(prev => {
            const next = new Set(prev)
            if (next.has(msg.id)) next.delete(msg.id)
            else next.add(msg.id)
            return next
          })}
          className="w-full py-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-50 hover:bg-emerald-100 border-t border-emerald-200 transition-colors"
        >
          {isFlipped ? '← Hide answer' : 'Reveal answer →'}
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  )
})()}
```

Wrap this in the messages loop so if `card` is null, the normal ReactMarkdown rendering runs as a fallback.

**Step D — Update the flashcard system prompt** in `app/api/chat/route.ts` to always output the structured format. Find the `flashcards` case in the mode prompt switch and add explicit format instructions:

```
Always format each flashcard exactly like this, with no deviation:

**Term:** [the term or concept]
**Definition:** [the definition or explanation]

Then ask "Got it? Type 'next' for another card, or tell me if you want me to explain further."
```

**Acceptance criteria:**
- In flashcard mode, AI responses formatted correctly render as a card with Term visible, Definition hidden
- Tapping "Reveal answer" shows Definition
- Tapping "← Hide answer" hides it again
- Malformed responses (conversational messages, explanations) fall back to standard bubble rendering
- `flippedCards` state resets when mode changes

