- `file`: a PDF, DOCX, or TXT file (max 10MB)
- `moduleNumber` (optional int)
- `moduleName` (optional string)
- `materialType` (optional string, default "syllabus")

Processing:
1. Validate file type (accept: `application/pdf`, `application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document`, `text/plain`, `text/markdown`).
2. For `.txt` and `.md`: read buffer directly as UTF-8 string.
3. For `.pdf`: use the `pdf-parse` npm package to extract text. Install it: `npm install pdf-parse`.
4. For `.docx`: use the `mammoth` npm package to extract raw text. Install it: `npm install mammoth`.
5. Truncate extracted text at 200,000 characters with a trailing note: `\n\n[Content truncated at upload limit]`.
6. Create a `CourseMaterial` record with:
   - `title`: the filename without extension, title-cased
   - `content`: extracted text
   - `materialType`: from body or "syllabus"
   - `moduleNumber`: from body or null
   - `moduleName`: from body or null
   - `isVisible`: true
   - `includeInAI`: true
7. Return the created `CourseMaterial` record.

