    "title": "string — concise title for this section",
    "content": "string — the full text of this section",
    "materialType": "syllabus|lecture|assignment|reading|rubric|quiz",
    "moduleName": "string — week or unit label, e.g. 'Week 1: Introduction' or null if not applicable",
    "moduleNumber": number or null
  }
]

Rules:
- Split at natural section boundaries (weeks, modules, units, major headings)
- Keep each section self-contained — do not omit content
- Assignments and grading rubrics should be separate entries from lecture content
- If the document is a single-page syllabus with no clear sections, return it as one entry
- Return only valid JSON, no explanation
```

Parse Claude's response as JSON. If parsing fails, return a 422 with `{ error: "Could not parse document structure", rawText }` so the client can fall back to a single-material entry.

Return the array of parsed materials (not yet saved). The client will display them for review before saving.

