## Architecture Notes

### What NOT to change

- **`ToolLaunchModal`** — the modal-first pattern for tool launching is correct. It lets users preview before committing to a full page navigation.
- **The Sandcastle experience cards** — these are the best-designed element on the page. Do not apply the compact card pattern to them.
- **The sticky filter bar** — `top-16 z-40` is correct. Do not change the sticky positioning.
- **The `allTools` / `tools` split** — fetching all tools once for smart sections and re-fetching for the browse grid (with filters) is the right architecture. Don't merge these into a single fetch.

### State Architecture — No Changes Required

The page's state is already well-structured:
- `allTools` — full unfiltered list for smart sections
- `tools` — filtered+paginated list for browse grid
- `allLoading` / `loading` — separate loading states for the two datasets
- `libraryIds` — Set for O(1) library membership checks

The only addition is `offset` and `loadingMore` for the "Load more" feature (Change 8).

### Component Extraction (Future Work)

When this page exceeds ~1,200 lines (currently ~1,060), extract into:
- `components/tools/FeaturedSection.tsx`
- `components/tools/CollectionStrip.tsx` (shared by Campus Navigator + Research Hub strips)
- `components/tools/BrowseGrid.tsx`
- `components/tools/SandcastleTab.tsx`

Do not extract prematurely — the current single-file structure is still maintainable.

