### Ghost Code / Candidates for Removal
These files exist but are no longer actively called (verify before deleting):
- **`app/components/BuildHubHero.tsx`** — orphaned; not imported by any page (explicitly noted in Build Hub section above)
- **`app/lib/document-processor.ts`** and **`app/lib/document-chunker.ts`** — RAG pipeline; built but not wired to any live route yet. Keep until avatar UI is built.
- **`app/lib/embedding-service.ts`** and **`app/lib/vector-store.ts`** — same; RAG infrastructure awaiting avatar UI.
- **`app/lib/ux-audit.ts`** + **`app/components/admin/UxAuditRunner.tsx`** — used only by `/admin/ux-audit`; low priority but active.
- **`/api/dashboard/`** — route is built and queries real DB data. However `page.tsx` still uses hardcoded `EDUCATOR_PROFILES` as the primary data source; the real API response is fetched in a useEffect but the synthetic data dominates the visible UI. Fully connecting the page to the live endpoint is still pending.

### What NOT to rebuild
- Tool data model is solid — extend it, don't replace it
- Prisma v7 + Neon driver adapter pattern works well in serverless; do not revert to `url` in datasource
- Keep mock auth demo mode even in production
- The user-switcher is a feature — reframe it, don't remove it
- Analytics synthetic data is fine for demos — label it honestly and build real data in sprint
- Sandcastle/Leagues — framing text added; don't redesign them

### Estimated team for production
- 1 senior full-stack engineer (Next.js + Prisma)
- 1 AI/ML engineer (embeddings, RAG, prompt engineering)
- 1 frontend engineer (UI polish, mobile, accessibility)
- 1 DevOps (Vercel, Neon, monitoring, FERPA compliance)
